│ Okay, let's address this persistent issue.   │
│ Based on the provided context – specifically │
│ the bug report highlighting Sphinx's         │
│ inability to document methods decorated with │
│ both @classmethod and @property – and the    │
│ search results indicating that Python 3.9+   │
│ handles these cases differently, the core    │
│ problem lies in how Sphinx is interpreting   │
│ the type of the returned object from these   │
│ combined decorators. The bug report suggests │
│ that Sphinx is incorrectly assuming the      │
│ return type is property when it should be    │
│ the actual class type.                       │
│                                              │
│ The fix involves ensuring that Sphinx        │
│ correctly identifies the type of the         │
│ returned object.  Since Python 3.9+ handles  │
│ these cases differently, the existing        │
│ documentation generation process isn't       │
│ properly accounting for this change.  A      │
│ simple adjustment to the documentation       │
│ generation process will resolve this.        │
│                                              │
│ Here's the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]docs/source/dummy_module.submodule.p  │
│  /file]                                      │
│  [original]                                  │
│  class MetaClass:                            │
│      metaclass_class_property =              │
│  property("class_property",                  │
│  "class_property_func", "class_property_doc  │
│  "MetaClass")                                │
│      metaclass_abstract_class_property =     │
│  property("abstract_class_property",         │
│  "abstract_class_property_func",             │
│  "abstract_class_property_doc", "MetaClass"  │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  class MetaClass:                            │
│      metaclass_class_property =              │
│  property("class_property",                  │
│  "class_property_func", "class_property_doc  │
│  MetaClass)                                  │
│      metaclass_abstract_class_property =     │
│  property("abstract_class_property",         │
